# ADT constructor type enforcement: [Error 42] should produce a type warning
# because Error expects String but receives Int(42).
# The [Ok 42] call is valid — Ok is polymorphic on `a`.
# Eval proceeds regardless of type errors (advisory).
[
  Result: [type [let a] [Ok a] [Error String]]
  ok-val:  [Ok 42]
  err-bad: [Error 42]
]
=== out
Dict({"Result": Dict({"Ok": Function(), "Error": Function()}), "ok-val": Variant(Result.Ok, Int(42)), "err-bad": Variant(Result.Error, Int(42))})

